2. DETAILED BREAKDOWN OF SYSTEM LAYERS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

LAYER 1: NATIVE NETWORK INTERCEPTION (JAVA / ANDROID OS)
- Primary Files:
  * app/src/main/java/com/privacy/browser/PrivacyWebViewClient.java
  * app/src/main/java/com/privacy/browser/adblock/AdBlockManager.java
  * app/src/main/java/com/privacy/browser/TrackerBlocker.java
  * app_files/adblock/network/hosts.txt (app storage)
  * app/src/main/assets/filters/hosts.txt (bootstrap template)
- Operation:
  * Overrides WebViewClient.shouldInterceptRequest(WebView, WebResourceRequest).
  * Every request (CSS, JS, images, font, iframe, media, XHR, fetch) is inspected
    at native Java speed prior to network transmission.
  * Performs parent-domain and sub-domain parsing against blockedHosts set (O(1)
    hash lookups for domains like doubleclick.net, googlesyndication.com, etc.).
  * Recognizes YouTube video ad endpoints (/api/stats/ads, /pagead/, adformat=).
  * Supports per-site toggles: NoScript, font blocking, large media blocking.
  * Synchronously updates blocked request counters and statistics exposed in
    AdBlockDashboardDialog.

LAYER 2: SYNTHETIC BENIGN RESPONSE ENGINE (ANTI-ERROR PLACEHOLDER)
- Primary File:
  * app/src/main/java/com/privacy/browser/PrivacyWebViewClient.java
- Problem Addressed:
  * Standard ad blockers returning 403 Forbidden or dropping connections cause
    Chromium to display its built-in "Webpage not available" error box inside
    ad iframes, leaving visible broken error frames on the page.
- Implementation:
  * Every blocked request returns HTTP 200 OK with WebResourceResponse and benign
    typed payloads matching the expected content type:
    1. Images: 1x1 transparent PNG byte array (image/png).
    2. Scripts: "/* blocked by privacy shield */" (application/javascript).
    3. Stylesheets: "/* blocked */" (text/css).
    4. APIs / XHR: "{}" (application/json).
    5. Main-Frame: Clean informative HTML block notification page.
    6. Subframes / Iframes: Self-collapsing, zero-dimension HTML document:
       "<!DOCTYPE html><html><head><style>html,body{display:none!important;visibility:hidden!important;margin:0!important;padding:0!important;width:0!important;height:0!important;overflow:hidden!important;border:none!important;}</style></head><body></body></html>"
  * Injects matching CORS headers (Access-Control-Allow-Origin, Access-Control-Allow-Credentials: true)
    so single-page applications do not throw synthetic CORS exceptions.

LAYER 3: DOM DEFUSION & COSMETIC PRUNING (DOCUMENT-START INJECTION)
- Primary File:
  * app/src/main/java/com/privacy/browser/adblock/AntiAdblockDefuser.java
  * app_files/adblock/scripts/anti_adblock.js
  * app_files/adblock/scripts/cosmetic_pruner.js
- Operation:
  * Injected at onPageStarted() (document_start) to precede publisher scripts.
  * Anti-Adblock Shims:
    - window.adsbygoogle = { loaded: true, push: function(obj) {} };
    - window.google_ad_client = "ca-pub-0000000000000000";
    - window.canRunAds = true;
    - window.isAdBlockActive = false;
  * Honeypot Bait Handling:
    - Neutralizes anti-adblock detection scripts looking for collapsed dummy elements.
  * Exact Container Collapse:
    - Targets specific ad wrappers (.adHolder, .adHolder.mpu, div[id^="mpu_"],
      .dmg-ads-ad, .dmg-ads-container, .billboard-container, .connatix-placeholder,
      .taboola, .outbrain) with:
      display: none !important;
      height: 0 !important;
      min-height: 0 !important;
      max-height: 0 !important;
      margin: 0 !important;
      padding: 0 !important;
      border: none !important;
  * Content Protection Guards:
    - Explicitly skips root article elements:
      if (node.tagName === 'ARTICLE' || node.tagName === 'MAIN' ||
          node.tagName === 'SECTION' || node.querySelector('p.mol-para-with-font')) continue;
    - Prevents false-positive hiding of article text paragraphs annotated with publisher
      ad-marker attributes (e.g. Daily Mail is="ad-marker-p").
  * MutationObserver:
    - Observes childList additions to body and dynamically prunes late-loaded ad slots.

LAYER 4: SPECIALIZED DEFUSERS AND USER FILTER RULES
- Primary Files:
  * app/src/main/java/com/privacy/browser/adblock/PopupClickDefuser.java
  * app/src/main/java/com/privacy/browser/adblock/YouTubeAdDefuser.java
  * app/src/main/java/com/privacy/browser/adblock/rules/UserFiltersManager.java
- Popup & Clickjack Defuser:
  * Tracks user gesture timestamps (click, keydown, touchend).
  * Hooks window.open; aborts popup attempts lacking a recent user gesture (< 1500ms)
    or matching known aggressive popup ad networks (popads, exoclick, adcash, etc.).
  * Scans for and removes full-screen transparent clickjacking divs (high z-index,
    position: fixed/absolute, opacity: 0).
- YouTube In-Stream Ad Defuser:
  * Strips adPlacements, adSlots, and playerAds from window.ytInitialPlayerResponse.
  * Hooks JSON.parse and Response.prototype.json to sanitize video stream responses.
  * Fast-forwards video ads and clicks skip buttons if an ad bypasses initial filters.
- User Filters (uBlock Origin format):
  * Enables user-created network blocking (||host^), whitelisting (@@||host^),
    and cosmetic element rules (domain##selector).
  * Parses and caches rules per origin in UserFiltersManager.

LAYER 5: INTERACTIVE VISUAL ELEMENT PICKER & ZAPPER
- Primary Files:
  * app/src/main/java/com/privacy/browser/adblock/picker/ElementPickerEngine.java
  * app/src/main/java/com/privacy/browser/adblock/picker/ElementPickerBridge.java
  * app/src/main/java/com/privacy/browser/adblock/picker/ElementPickerDialog.java
- Interactive Picker Workflow:
  * Activated from toolbar or adblock menu. Injects ElementPickerEngine into WebView.
  * Renders a full-screen semi-transparent hovering inspector with red selection boundary
    and badge indicating the tag and dimensions of the targeted element.
  * Communicates via native JavascriptInterface (ElementPickerBridge) on element tap.
- ElementPickerDialog Capabilities:
  * Dynamic Opacity Slider: Interactive SeekBar at the top of the dialog allowing
    the user to adjust modal opacity from 10% (ultra-clear glass) to 100% (solid),
    letting them clearly view the underlying DOM element while configuring rules.
    Opacity preference is persisted in SharedPreferences (element_picker_prefs).
  * Rounded Specificity Chips: Generates candidate selectors (e.g. ID, class combinations,
    composite path, parent container) styled as selectable pills.
  * Custom Selector Input: Monospace input field for manual CSS tweaking.
  * Live Preview Toggle: "Preview" button temporarily hides or reveals the element
    in the live page to verify rule correctness before persisting.
  * Create Rule: Appends the rule (e.g. example.com##div.banner-ad) directly into
    UserFiltersManager and persists it to app_files/adblock/cosmetic/cosmetic_rules.txt.
- Element Zapper Workflow:
  * Immediate one-shot mode: user taps an element, and it is instantly pruned from
    the live DOM without opening the dialog or persisting permanent filter rules.

LAYER 6: DYNAMIC CUSTOM USER SCRIPTLET ENGINE
- Primary Files:
  * app/src/main/java/com/privacy/browser/adblock/UserScriptManager.java
  * app/src/main/java/com/privacy/browser/adblock/AdBlockFileManager.java
  * app/src/main/res/layout/dialog_create_user_script.xml
  * app_files/adblock/user_scripts/*.js
- Capabilities:
  * Enables users to create, edit, toggle, and delete standalone custom JavaScript
    scriptlets directly within the browser without rebuilding or recompiling.
  * Header Metadata Parsing:
    - // @name         Scriptlet display name
    - // @run-at       document-start | document-end
    - // @match        URL wildcard pattern (*, *youtube.com*, <all_urls>)
    - // @enabled      true | false
- Dual-Timing Injection Pipeline:
  * document-start: Injected via WebViewCompat.addDocumentStartJavaScript and onPageStarted
    prior to any webpage scripts executing. Essential for API hooks, defusers, and stubs.
  * document-end: Injected via evaluateJavascript in onPageFinished after the DOM is ready.
    Ideal for MutationObserver hooks, late cosmetic pruning, and DOM modifications.
- Scriptlet Creation Modal & Presets:
  * Spacious responsive container (min 92% screen width, capped at 520dp).
  * 6 Built-In Starter Presets & Hook Templates:
    1. Blank Scriptlet: Clean IIFE boilerplate for generic adblock logic.
    2. window.open (Popups): Intercepts and sanitizes window.open to suppress popups.
    3. ytInitialPlayerResponse (YouTube): Defuses in-stream video ads before player init.
    4. adsbygoogle (Anti-Adblock): Stubs adsbygoogle array and bait detection probes.
    5. fetch / XHR (Network): Hooks fetch and XMLHttpRequest to filter tracking payloads.
    6. MutationObserver (DOM): Real-time observer to detect and prune dynamic ad elements.
  * Automated defaults: selecting any preset pre-populates the filename, target @match,
    recommended lifecycle timing, and production-grade boilerplate.

LAYER 7: CLOUD STATE SYNCHRONIZATION & SNAPSHOT VERSIONING
- Primary Files:
  * app/src/main/java/com/privacy/browser/adblock/cloud/AdBlockCloudClient.java
  * app/src/main/java/com/privacy/browser/adblock/cloud/AdBlockDiffEngine.java
  * app/src/main/java/com/privacy/browser/adblock/cloud/AdBlockCloudStatesDialog.java
- Functionality:
  * Backs up and synchronizes user adblock rules, custom hosts, cosmetic filters,
    and user scriptlets to Cloudflare KV storage.
  * Displays visual commit history with timestamps, commit messages, and author hashes.
  * Differential Inspection: side-by-side or line-by-line diff view showing added,
    modified, or deleted rules across state snapshots.
  * Rollback & Restore: Allows rolling back to any historical snapshot or performing
    differential merge restores without overwriting unaffected local rules.
  * Zero-knowledge token storage: API keys and account credentials securely saved in
    private SharedPreferences.

