3. APP STORAGE & FILE SYSTEM ARCHITECTURE
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
All ad blocking components reside in the app-private internal storage directory:
  context.getFilesDir() / adblock /

Directory Structure:
  adblock/
  |-- network/
  |   `-- hosts.txt               <-- Active network blocklist (hostnames)
  |-- cosmetic/
  |   `-- cosmetic_rules.txt      <-- Active cosmetic element hiding rules
  |-- scripts/
  |   |-- anti_adblock.js         <-- Built-in anti-adblock shim and bait stubs
  |   |-- cosmetic_pruner.js      <-- Built-in cosmetic DOM pruning script
  |   |-- popups.js               <-- Built-in popup and overlay defuser
  |   `-- youtube.js              <-- Built-in YouTube player ad defuser
  `-- user_scripts/
      |-- popup_interceptor.js    <-- User custom scriptlet
      |-- yt_ad_defuser.js        <-- User custom scriptlet
      `-- *.js                    <-- Additional standalone user scriptlets

Asset Bootstrapping:
- On first launch, AdBlockFileManager checks if app_files/adblock exists.
- If missing, it copies baseline templates from assets/filters/ into app storage.
- If assets are newer than storage files, it performs automated non-destructive updates.
- All modifications made via the in-app editor or element picker persist in storage
  and survive app updates.

